{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"id":"CircleCI.CLI","latestVersion":"1.14.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"copyright":"Circle Internet Services, Inc.","description":"CircleCI command line tool.","installationNotes":"To enable PowerShell tab-completion, register the completions from your\nPowerShell profile ($PROFILE). The first command ensures the profile's\nparent directory exists (Add-Content creates the file but not the folder);\nthe second appends the registration line:\n\n  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path (Split-Path $PROFILE) -Force | Out-Null\n  Add-Content -Path $PROFILE -Value 'circleci completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression'\n","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/CircleCI-Public/circleci-cli/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"copyright":"Circle Internet Services, Inc.","description":"CircleCI command line tool.","installationNotes":"To enable PowerShell tab-completion, register the completions from your\nPowerShell profile ($PROFILE). The first command ensures the profile's\nparent directory exists (Add-Content creates the file but not the folder);\nthe second appends the registration line:\n\n  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path (Split-Path $PROFILE) -Force | Out-Null\n  Add-Content -Path $PROFILE -Value 'circleci completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression'\n","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/CircleCI-Public/circleci-cli/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"`circleci` is CircleCI's official command line tool. It is an agent-friendly CLI that brings CI runs, jobs,\nconfiguration, and other CircleCI features to the terminal right where you're already working.\n","moniker":"CircleCI CLI","name":"CircleCI CLI","packageUrl":"https://circleci.com/","publisher":"CircleCI","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/CircleCI-Public/circleci-cli/issues/new","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/CircleCI-Public","releaseNotes":"What's Changed\n- TEST-376 Add device and user ID to extension env by @liamclarkedev in #1959\n- Stamp source builds with git describe so they aren't nagged to upgrade by @gcirclest in #1958\n- Escape markdown in function get and list output by @stiyyagura0901 in #1961\n- Point AI coding agents to CircleCI's skills (AEX-82) by @joel-thompson in #1968","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/CircleCI-Public/circleci-cli/releases/tag/v1.14.0","tags":["circle-ci","circleci","cli","command-line-tool","continuous-delivery","continuous-integration","developer-tools","devops","golang","graphql","tool"]}},"longDescription":"`circleci` is CircleCI's official command line tool. It is an agent-friendly CLI that brings CI runs, jobs,\nconfiguration, and other CircleCI features to the terminal right where you're already working.\n","moniker":"CircleCI CLI","name":"CircleCI CLI","packageUrl":"https://circleci.com/","publisher":"CircleCI","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/CircleCI-Public/circleci-cli/issues/new","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/CircleCI-Public","releaseNotes":"What's Changed\n- TEST-376 Add device and user ID to extension env by @liamclarkedev in #1959\n- Stamp source builds with git describe so they aren't nagged to upgrade by @gcirclest in #1958\n- Escape markdown in function get and list output by @stiyyagura0901 in #1961\n- Point AI coding agents to CircleCI's skills (AEX-82) by @joel-thompson in #1968","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/CircleCI-Public/circleci-cli/releases/tag/v1.14.0","tags":["circle-ci","circleci","cli","command-line-tool","continuous-delivery","continuous-integration","developer-tools","devops","golang","graphql","tool"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.14.0/app.json","detailSha256":"a8467d87af1424f15c9059ce05ebeabb1dcc0b417b5f2445457bc014ceae6fc6","releaseDate":"2026-11-04","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"1.14.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"ve